A6_ADBD_E1110B8915B9_171815.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"concall_transcript","date":"2016-06-01","title":"Jun 2016 Concall Transcript","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=D669DA03_0C56_4242_83B5_EDBCBFF38F90_161839.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2026","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=551ebf5b-4234-41c2-b934-e1ebf5034199.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2025","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/f4bb012f-0505-4707-a590-b2cf4e837c37.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2024","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/23c502f1-4478-4bd0-95c0-d6b680cd7207.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2023","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/a4a9e70f-019e-43d0-b0f1-ef6a9ec816ad.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2022","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/73714532259.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2021","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/68896532259_15_07_21.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2020","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590320.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2019","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590319.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2018","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590318.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2017","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590317.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2016","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590316.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2015","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590315.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2014","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590314.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2013","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532259/5322590313.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2012","url":"https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/AR_APARINDS_2011_2012_18102012054545.zip","source":"the data provider"}],"analysis":{"summary":"APAR Industries reported its highest-ever quarterly sales and profit for Q1 FY27, with consolidated revenues growing by 29.1% year-on-year to reach INR6,591 crores and PAT increasing by 77.7% to INR467 crores. EBITDA post open period forex surged by 62.7% to INR814 crores, driven by higher sales realizations and unit profitability across all three operating divisions. Management highlighted that despite external challenges such as the U.S.-Iran war, logistics disruptions, and manpower shortages in May, strong execution discipline helped deliver robust financial results. The company also announced pending order books of INR10,190 crores for the conductor division and INR1,925 crores for the cable division. Apar Industries Limited reported its financial results and operational updates for the first quarter ended June 30, 2026.","themes":{"guidance":[],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"New order inflow from the US has started to increase in the cable division.","quote":"New order inflow from US has started to increase.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"Management stated that the structural energy infrastructure fundamentals remain robust, supported by growth in T&D, rising electricity demand, and increasing evacuation infrastructure.","quote":"However, having said that, structurally, energy infrastructure fundamentals remain intact with the growth in T&D, rising electricity demand and evacuation infrastructure being increased, data center expansion, the growing presence of EVs, more opportunities for reconducting and upgradation of aging lines and, finally, the significant investment happening in ultra-high voltage transmission infrastructure and HVDC.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"Management noted that the Middle East business will remain somewhat subdued until the ongoing war is resolved.","quote":"So I see that the Middle East business will continue to remain a little bit subdued until this war gets completed.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"The company anticipates a short-term slowdown in ordering due to significantly higher metal prices, increased premiums, and elevated freight costs.","quote":"See, one thing, Nitin, I'll add to this is that there is still -- whether it's the U.S. or whether it's India, there is a short-term slowdown in ordering because especially with aluminum, aluminum moves along with the cost of energy.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"The company plans to increase its capital expenditure for FY27 to about INR1,500 crores, following an expenditure of INR740 crores in FY26.","quote":"We plan to increase our capex for FY27 to about INR1,500 crores in addition to the FY26 capex that we have incurred of INR740 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"The planned capex breakup for FY27 includes around INR400 crores from the conductor division, around INR200-odd crores from the oil division, and approximately INR850 crores from the cable division.","quote":"Around INR400 crores would be coming from conductor division, around INR200-odd crores on oil division, and cable would be in the range of INR850 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"The company provided approximately INR94 crores for the oil division in the quarter in line with accounting standards due to sharp rises and falls in crude and gas oil prices.","quote":"So, with the price of crude oil and gas oil having risen very sharply at the beginning of the quarter and then falling quite sharply at the end of the period, the company has followed the requirements of accounting standards and has provided for approximately INR94 crores for the oil division in the quarter.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"The oil division's EBITDA margins came in at a substantially higher level of INR25,482 per kL compared to INR7,004 per kL a year ago.","quote":"However, post taking this provision into account, the EBITDA margins came in at a substantially higher level of INR25,482 per kL compared to INR7,004 per kL a year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"Conductor division absolute EBITDA grew to INR53,418 per ton compared to INR43,688 per ton a year earlier.","quote":"EBITDA growth is attributable to a higher share of the premium mix due to which despite a slightly lower volume of conventional conductors, the absolute EBITDA has grown, which came in at INR53,418 per ton compared to INR43,688 per ton a year earlier.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"Cable division EBITDA post open ForEx came in at INR194 crores, up 36.7% with a margin of 10.6%.","quote":"EBITDA post open ForEx came in at INR194 crores, which is up 36.7%. The EBITDA margin has come in at 10.6% in Q1, which is up by 60 basis points over a year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"A provision of Rs 93 crores has been made in line with prudent compliance and accounting standard requirements.","quote":"In line with prudent compliance and requirement of accounting standards, a provision of Rs 93 crores has been made.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"Management noted that the increase in metal prices will lead to higher interest costs, which impacts the overall earnings before interest.","quote":"Also to note is that with the increase in the metal prices, you will see higher interest costs also coming in because the metal price is going up.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"One-time provisions in the fourth quarter included gratuity and leave encashment, a mark-to-market impact of an ECB loan due to rupee depreciation, and an old legal case provision.","quote":"That includes an impact of gratuity and leave encashment, which we have further increased by approximately INR8 crores. There is a mark-to-market impact of an ECB loan that the company has due to the sharp depreciation of the rupee that happened in the first quarter. And then there is a one-off provision for an old legal case based on the recommendations of our auditors that we have moved from contingent liabilities into a provision.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"The conductor division's pending order book stands at around INR10,190 crores with an export proportion of 56.8%.","quote":"The pending order book stands at around INR10,190 crores with an export proportion of 56.8%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"New orders received by the conductor division were INR5,245 crores in the quarter, with exports contributing 65.8%.","quote":"New orders received by the conductor division were INR5,245 crores in the quarter, of which exports contributed to 65.8%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"The cable division's pending order stands at INR1,925 crores compared to INR1,653 crores from a year ago.","quote":"The pending order today stands at INR1,925 crores. So it largely covers the plan or the requirement for the current -- for the coming quarter compared to INR1,653 crores from a year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"Pending order book for the conductor division was ₹ 10,190 crores, with exports contributing 56.8%.","quote":"Pending order book was ₹ 10,190 crores, of which exports contribute 56.8%","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"New orders received in the conductor division stood at ₹ 5,245 crores in Q1 FY27, with exports contributing 65.8%.","quote":"New order received stood at ₹ 5,245 crores in Q1 FY27 of which exports contribute 65.8%.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"Pending order book in the cable division is at ₹ 1,925 crores compared to Rs 1,653 crores a year ago.","quote":"Pending order book is at ₹ 1,925 crores compared to Rs 1,653 crores year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"The pending order book for the cable division remains at approximately INR1,800 crores.","quote":"The pending order remains at approximately INR1,800 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"Capacity utilization for the conductor division is currently between 90% and 95%.","quote":"Yes. So on the conductor division, our capacity utilization currently will be about 90% to 95%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"},{"claim":"Capacity utilization for the cable division is close to 85% to 90%.","quote":"And similarly, for cables, it could be close to about 85% to 90%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf"}],"capital_allocation":[],"risks_headwinds":[{"claim":"The quarter was challenging due to the impact of the U.S.-Iran war, logistics difficulties in export markets, and manpower shortages in May.","quote":"Otherwise, this has been a fairly challenging quarter from an external perspective, given the impact of the U.S.-Iran war, various logistics difficulties that have happened in the export markets and fairly significant manpower-related shortages in the month of May, which coincided with holidays as well as local elections.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"Conductor volumes were down 6.7% due to a surge in metal prices impacting delivery schedules where customers withheld manufacturing clearance.","quote":"Volume for the quarter was down 6.7% compared to a year ago. This can be attributed fundamentally to a surge in the metal prices that have impacted delivery schedules of orders which are in hand, where customers have withheld manufacturing clearance, especially due to the sudden increase in the price of aluminum and where customers were not having hedged metal.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"Oil division volumes were affected because the UAE facility was restricted to making local deliveries due to the crisis and resulting closure of the Hamriyah port.","quote":"Volume for the quarter stands at 129,085 kL, down 13.7% compared to a year ago and down -- yes, the volumes were affected really because of our facility in the UAE, which because of this crisis and the resulting closure of the Hamriyah port was restricted to only making local deliveries of the product that it had in inventory.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=cf387166-2aa9-45c6-b5cc-b6f7222f928f.pdf"},{"claim":"A surge in metal prices impacted order booking and delivery schedules for orders in hand.","quote":"Surge in metal prices impacted order booking and delivery schedule of orders in hand","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"Volumes at the UAE facility were lower mainly due to the Middle East crisis resulting in the closure of Hamriyah port.","quote":"Volumes were lower at our UAE facility mainly due to the middle east crisis resulting in closure of Hamriyah port.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"},{"claim":"Lower allocation by oil suppliers in the month of April affected volumes.","quote":"Also lower allocation by oil suppliers in the month of April affected volumes, which however, got restored subsequently.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf"}]},"management_commitments":[{"claim":"Large orders exceeding ₹ 2,800 crores from two major overseas electric utility companies have a delivery period spread over the next 4 years.","quote":"This includes large orders exceeding ₹ 2,800 crores from two major overseas electric utility companies with a delivery period spread over next 4 years reinforcing the investments behind transmission capex globally","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d13afc5e-4810-4775-b6e5-977bf448a07d.pdf","timeframe":"next 2 years"},{"claim":"Management stated that from a medium to long-term perspective, conductor margins are expected to be in the range of INR35,000 to INR36,000 per metric ton plus tailwinds.","quote":"And based on the historical EBITDA margin that we have made, we expect that from a medium to long-term perspective, our conductor margins could be in the range of INR35,000 to INR36,000 per metric ton.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf","timeframe":""},{"claim":"The company plans to increase its capital expenditure for FY27 to about INR1,500 crores.","quote":"We plan to increase our capex for FY27 to about INR1,500 crores in addition to the FY26 capex that we have incurred of INR740 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-06-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7d1b406e-5f03-4c54-9d98-0abf6608d0d8.pdf","timeframe":"FY27"}],"coverage":{"docs_analysed":3,"kinds":["concall_transcript","concall_ppt"]}},"_meta":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash","grounded":true,"facts_kept":31,"facts_dropped_ungrounded":4,"note":"Facts are verbatim-grounded against the company's own documents; claims whose quote was not found were dropped."}}